            <ArticleTitle>Aneurysmal formation after successful pulsed laser coronary angioplasty.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>125-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report two cases of coronary artery aneurysmal formation as long term consequences of Ho:YAG and excimer laser coronary angioplasty. This case report suggests that pulsed laser angioplasty may result in severe vessel wall damage that may lead ultimately to aneurysmal formation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
